from pathlib import Path
def edit(path, fn):
 p=Path(path);p.write_text(fn(p.read_text(encoding='utf-8')),encoding='utf-8')
summary='**1.8.5 local candidate — configurable concurrent evidence requests.** Management → Service → **Concurrent requests…** sets an even value from **4 to 64**, default **16**. MCP admission, a pool of independent native evidence channels and project-worker processing use the same setting, with one additional status/control slot. Changes apply to subsequent requests without restarting agents; accepted work drains when the value decreases. Sources, revision identity and typed retry rules remain authoritative. See the [1.8.5 candidate record](docs/releases/release-1.8.5.md) for validation and manual installer identity.\n\n'
edit('README.md',lambda s:s.replace('**1.8.4 development candidate — more direct identifier investigations.**',summary+'**Earlier 1.8.4 candidate — more direct identifier investigations.**',1).replace('source versions are synchronized at **1.8.4**','source versions are synchronized at **1.8.5**'))
edit('packages/vscode/README.md',lambda s:s.replace('**1.8.4 development candidate:**',summary.replace('(docs/releases/release-1.8.5.md)','(https://github.com/iokaio/airk/blob/main/docs/releases/release-1.8.5.md)')+'**Earlier 1.8.4 candidate:**',1).replace('synchronized at **1.8.4**','synchronized at **1.8.5**'))
edit('docs/README.md',lambda s:s.replace('# AIRK documentation','# AIRK documentation\n\n**1.8.5 local candidate:** [configurable request capacity](releases/release-1.8.5.md), default 16 and even values 4–64, connects Management → Service to MCP admission, independent native channels and project processing. Qualification is recorded with the candidate.',1).replace('**1.8.4 development:**','**Earlier 1.8.4 development:**',1).replace('synchronized at **1.8.4**','synchronized at **1.8.5**').replace('synchronized at 1.8.4','synchronized at 1.8.5'))
edit('docs/releases/README.md',lambda s:s.replace('- [1.8.4]', '- [1.8.5](./release-1.8.5.md): configurable concurrent evidence requests and matching native channel/project capacity; unpublished manual-test candidate\n- [1.8.4]',1))
edit('CONTRIBUTING.md',lambda s:s.replace('**1.8.4**','**1.8.5**').replace('--expected 1.8.4','--expected 1.8.5'))
edit('docs/architecture.md',lambda s:s.replace('# Architecture\n','# Architecture\n\nIn 1.8.5, Core defines the validated 4–64 even concurrency contract (default 16); the existing CLI service resource adapter persists it. Management → Service edits that policy. MCP admission observes it before each request, and the CLI leases independent authenticated channels from a bounded pool. The supervisor grants the same evidence concurrency plus one status/control slot to each worker and acknowledges live updates before saving them. Worker-local broker admission bounds actual requests across clients. The shared materialization lifetime gate retains accepted blocking work through rendering/accounting and cancellation under a finite 65-slot ceiling; the broker supplies the configured limit. Shrinking capacity drains accepted charges. Collection scope, native authority and publication contracts are preserved.\n',1))
for f in ['docs/mcp-developer-guide.md','docs/cli-developer-guide.md']:
 edit(f,lambda s:s.replace('1.8.4 development candidate','1.8.5 development candidate').replace('[1.8.4 release record](releases/release-1.8.4.md)','[1.8.5 release record](releases/release-1.8.5.md)'))
edit('docs/mcp-developer-guide.md',lambda s:s.replace("Four is the bridge's concurrent-call cap, not a guarantee that four simultaneous calls bypass downstream setup/admission.", 'Concurrent evidence capacity defaults to 16 and is configurable in Management → Service from 4 to 64 in even steps. Matching native channels and project processing have the same allowance; status has one additional slot. A bounded 128-request queue absorbs brief contention, but downstream setup, ownership and deadlines can still refuse unsubmitted work.'))
edit('docs/service-protocol.md',lambda s:s.replace('It admits one query and 64 KiB of response credit to each resident worker;', 'It admits the configured concurrent evidence requests (default 16; even values 4–64) plus one status/control slot, with 64 KiB of response credit per admitted request, to each resident worker;'))
edit('docs/service-resources.md',lambda s:s+'\n## Concurrent evidence requests in 1.8.5\n\nManagement → Service → Concurrent requests… sets `query_concurrency`: default 16, even values 4–64. Existing saved policies without the field use 16. The setting is service-host-wide; each project receives the same request allowance, shared across its callers. Each MCP frontend uses a matching native channel pool; independent clients cannot multiply the worker allowance. One additional status/control slot remains available alongside evidence capacity. Larger concurrency permits more simultaneous work and can increase memory/CPU demand; request bytes, grants, resource observations and bounded refusal contracts still apply. This is a concurrency setting, not a throughput guarantee or an OS hard memory limit.\n\nNative workers acknowledge changes before the service saves the new value. MCP frontends observe it on subsequent requests. Reductions retain accepted charges until completion and stop further admissions above the new value. Idle surplus frontend channels are retired on subsequent use. Each relevant waiting stage is finite (128 waiting requests); cancellation or EOF cannot refund accepted blocking work early or cause replay.\n')
edit('packages/vscode/src/explorerHelp/manage-service.md',lambda s:s.replace('- Change the resource preset or custom limits.','- Set **Concurrent requests…** to an even number from **4 to 64** (default **16**). The same service-host setting controls MCP evidence admission, independent native channels and each project’s processing allowance. One status/control slot is reserved in addition. Changes apply to subsequent requests; accepted work drains after a decrease.\n- Change the resource preset or custom limits. Request capacity is preserved when changing presets.'))
for f in ['docs/mcp.md','docs/unified-mcp.md','docs/vscode-extension.md']:
 edit(f,lambda s:s+'\n## Concurrent evidence requests (1.8.5)\n\nManagement → Service → Concurrent requests… sets the service-host policy: default 16, even values 4–64. MCP admission, independent native channel pools and project-worker processing use the same allowance, with one extra status/control slot. Native owners acknowledge live changes before the policy is saved; subsequent frontend requests observe it. Reductions drain accepted work, and finite queues and typed unsubmitted retry receipts remain authoritative. See [service resources](service-resources.md#concurrent-evidence-requests-in-185) and [candidate validation](releases/release-1.8.5.md).\n')
# Tool guidance is current executable documentation, unlike dated scenario records.
for f in ['crates/airk-mcp/src/response.rs','crates/airk-mcp/src/unified.rs']:
 edit(f,lambda s:s.replace('Bridge cap 4; downstream may refuse.', 'Evidence capacity defaults to 16; Management Service allows even values 4..64. Native channels/project processing match; one extra status slot. Downstream may refuse.'))
edit('packages/vscode/src/test/serviceConsole.test.ts',lambda s:s.replace("row.label==='Concurrent evidence requests'&&row.value===String(concurrency)","row[0]==='Concurrent evidence requests'&&row[1]===String(concurrency)"))
